strategy.change.about.consensus:
- **Change Over Time:** for each measure, the value of the 14 days ending at each of the last 26 week ends (line; the weeks are counted back from the time of calculation, not calendar weeks) and the 7-day value of the same weeks (faint dots, shown without comparison: 7 days is shorter than the 14 days the consensus recommends; Battelino et al., 2019), calculated hourly. The table compares the last 4 weeks with 9–13 and 22–26 weeks ago. A 14-day or 7-day value or a 4-week period with less than 70% sensor active has no value (--- in the table, a gap in the line); the differences and the direction are calculated for every period with at least 70% sensor active, and the sensor-active row of the table shows the sensor active of each period that has enough data. GMI is shown only for periods of 14 days or more with at least 70% sensor active (Battelino et al., 2019; Bergenstal et al., 2018). This method is a GlucoCraft rule.
- **Direction:** whether the last 4 weeks are higher or lower than 22–26 weeks ago (or 9–13 weeks ago when 22–26 weeks ago has less than 70% sensor active), or *No change* when the difference rounds to zero; a numerical difference without clinical interpretation. This method is a GlucoCraft rule. The consensus target (Battelino et al., 2019) is shown separately. {cx_dagger}
- **Backgrounds of the charts:** green within the consensus target (Battelino et al., 2019), red outside it, divided exactly at it; neutral gray where no consensus target exists.

strategy.consensus.about:
- **Layout:** the core measures first (time in range, time in tight range, time below 70 mg/dL (3.9 mmol/L), time below 54 mg/dL (3.0 mmol/L), time above 180 mg/dL (10.0 mmol/L)), then their change over time; all other measures and periods are behind the *Show All Statistics* button at the bottom of the page.
- **Ranges:** the international consensus ranges for continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) data (Battelino et al., 2019) and the tight range 70–140 mg/dL = 3.9–7.8 mmol/L (Battelino et al., 2023), irrespective of the settings.
- **Statistics:** all seven periods side by side. ✓ / ✗ indicate whether a value meets its published consensus target (Battelino et al., 2019); an arithmetic comparison, not a clinical assessment. A warning above the table names each period with less than 70% sensor active.
