- {cx_active}
- {cx_above}
- {cx_cv} {cx_cv_primary}
- {cx_per_day}
- **GMI** (Bergenstal et al., 2018) is an estimate, not a laboratory A1C. {cx_gmi_days}
- {cx_gri}
- **Calculation** (calculated by GlucoCraft): statistics are weighted by time, not by the number of readings; gaps (see *Graphs*) are excluded. Readings at the sensor's limit (LO / HI) are left out of the mean, standard deviation, CV, GMI and the lowest and highest values, and counted as very low or very high in the time in ranges; a CGM manufacturer's report software shows such readings at the limit (Abbott Diabetes Care, 2018); no consensus document addresses them, and their number and time are stated under the table. This method is a GlucoCraft rule. Each period ends at the present time and is recalculated every 5 minutes.
- **Graphs:** plotted by measurement time. Every graph is interrupted at a gap: an interval between two readings that is longer than 15 minutes or three reading intervals, whichever is longer, the reading interval being the median of the 10 intervals before the reading (the higher of the two middle values). This method is a GlucoCraft rule. The 7- and 14-day graphs show the mean and range of each time slot. A LO / HI reading has no value and interrupts the line. The scale follows the data; the background bands are the consensus ranges.
- **Data:** `sensor.glucocraft_<period>_consensus_ranges` (one entity per period).
